{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1782045372115,"sessionID":"ses_115d3aef6ffeMbIUsJnnq6Fzvd","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_03a7b69efb1c47959b45a3c3","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"package com.example.books;\n\nimport org.junit.jupiter.api.AfterEach;\nimport org.junit.jupiter.api.BeforeEach;\nimport org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;\n\nimport java.io.IOException;\nimport java.sql.SQLException;\n\nimport static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.assertEquals;\nimport static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.assertTrue;\n\nclass BookApiIntegrationTest {\n\n    private TestServer server;\n\n    @BeforeEach\n    void setUp() throws IOException, SQLException {\n        server = new TestServer();\n    }\n\n    @AfterEach\n    void tearDown() {\n        if (server != null) server.close();\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    void healthReturnsOk() throws IOException, InterruptedException {\n        var resp = server.send(\"GET\", \"/health\", null);\n        assertEquals(200, resp.statusCode());\n        assertEquals(\"{\\\"status\\\":\\\"ok\\\"}\", resp.body());\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    void createListGetUpdateDeleteLifecycle() throws IOException, InterruptedException {\n        String payload = \"{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Dune\\\",\\\"author\\\":\\\"Frank Herbert\\\",\\\"year\\\":1965,\\\"isbn\\\":\\\"9780441172719\\\"}\";\n\n        var create = server.send(\"POST\", \"/books\", payload);\n        assertEquals(201, create.statusCode());\n        assertTrue(create.body().contains(\"\\\"id\\\":\"));\n        assertTrue(create.body().contains(\"\\\"title\\\":\\\"Dune\\\"\"));\n\n        var list = server.send(\"GET\", \"/books\", null);\n        assertEquals(200, list.statusCode());\n        assertTrue(list.body().startsWith(\"[\"));\n        assertTrue(list.body().contains(\"Dune\"));\n\n        long id = extractId(create.body());\n\n        var one = server.send(\"GET\", \"/books/\" + id, null);\n        assertEquals(200, one.statusCode());\n        assertTrue(one.body().contains(\"\\\"author\\\":\\\"Frank Herbert\\\"\"));\n\n        var update = server.send(\"PUT\", \"/books/\" + id,\n                \"{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Dune Updated\\\",\\\"author\\\":\\\"Frank Herbert\\\",\\\"year\\\":1965,\\\"isbn\\\":\\\"X\\\"}\");\n        assertEquals(200, update.statusCode());\n        assertTrue(update.body().contains(\"\\\"title\\\":\\\"Dune Updated\\\"\"));\n\n        var del = server.send(\"DELETE\", \"/books/\" + id, null);\n        assertEquals(204, del.statusCode());\n\n        var afterDelete = server.send(\"GET\", \"/books/\" + id, null);\n        assertEquals(404, afterDelete.statusCode());\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    void authorFilterAndValidationErrors() throws IOException, InterruptedException {\n        server.send(\"POST\", \"/books\", \"{\\\"title\\\":\\\"A\\\",\\\"author\\\":\\\"Alice\\\",\\\"year\\\":2001,\\\"isbn\\\":\\\"i1\\\"}\");\n        server.send(\"POST\", \"/books\", \"{\\\"title\\\":\\\"B\\\",\\\"author\\\":\\\"Bob\\\",\\\"year\\\":2002,\\\"isbn\\\":\\\"i2\\\"}\");\n\n        var filtered = server.send(\"GET\", \"/books?author=Alice\", null);\n        assertEquals(200, filtered.statusCode());\n        assertTrue(filtered.body().contains(\"\\\"author\\\":\\\"Alice\\\"\"));\n        assertTrue(!filtered.body().contains(\"\\\"author\\\":\\\"Bob\\\"\"));\n\n        var missingTitle = server.send(\"POST\", \"/books\",\n                \"{\\\"author\\\":\\\"NoTitle\\\"}\");\n        assertEquals(400, missingTitle.statusCode());\n        assertTrue(missingTitle.body().contains(\"title is required\"));\n\n        var missingAuthor = server.send(\"POST\", \"/books\",\n                \"{\\\"title\\\":\\\"NoAuthor\\\"}\");\n        assertEquals(400, missingAuthor.statusCode());\n        assertTrue(missingAuthor.body().contains(\"author is required\"));\n\n        var unknown = server.send(\"GET\", \"/books/99999\", null);\n        assertEquals(404, unknown.statusCode());\n    }\n\n    private static long extractId(String json) {\n        int idx = json.indexOf(\"\\\"id\\\":\");\n        int start = idx + 5;\n        int end = start;\n        while (end < json.length() && Character.isDigit(json.charAt(end))) end++;\n        return Long.parseLong(json.substring(start, end));\n    }\n}\n","filePath":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-z0i76flh/retort-ee7883aca8f1/src/test/java/com/example/books/BookApiIntegrationTest.java"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-z0i76flh/retort-ee7883aca8f1/src/test/java/com/example/books/BookApiIntegrationTest.java","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"src/test/java/com/example/books/BookApiIntegrationTest.java","time":{"start":1782045372109,"end":1782045372114}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Wait — for `:memory:` the URL would be `jdbc:sqlite::memory:`. My constructor does `\"jdbc:sqlite:\" + dbPath`, so dbPath = \":memory:\" yields \"jdbc:sqlite::memory:\". Good.\n\nAlso there's a subtle issue: in-memory SQLite + multi-threaded executor. The repository uses a single Connection, and concurrent access from multiple threads could be unsafe. SQLite JDBC connections are not thread-safe by default? Actually the driver synchronizes? Hmm. For tests using a single-threaded executor + HttpClient sequential, fine. But the HttpServer executor I set to single thread, so requests are sequential. Good.\n\nBut wait, the BookHandler in handle() reads body via JsonUtil.fromJson(exchange.getRequestBody(), Book.class) and also for update. Good.\n\nOne concern: in Main I use Executors.newFixedThreadPool(8). For tests I use single thread. Fine.\n\nLet me write the actual tests now.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eea2e5701001ZL9s8F7v1CeKBt","sessionID":"ses_115d3aef6ffeMbIUsJnnq6Fzvd","messageID":"msg_eea2e4a8b001b5L9PQon5iBjDk"}}
